+// A confirmed abort decision (the declarations' region near the top says what it is) goes to the peers as record 57 and
+// to a later incarnation in its activation blob, and a receiver applies it once its own view of the target allows it:
+//   - the log: every rank keeps an append-only log of the decisions it made or took (key: decider rank, its incarnation,
+//     its decision number from 1). The watcher only adds its own entry (gdakiHoldWatchdog); sending, receiving, checking
+//     and applying are the helper's (the spare's driver stores the activation blob's entries before its helper runs);
+//   - sending: to every peer whose lineage is LIVE here and whose record channel is up, never to the target or to the
+//     decider's own incarnation. A peer's send key is (its incarnation, its record channel's generation); the first key
+//     takes what this rank had then as known to it, a later key (a new incarnation paired, a QP regeneration that drops
+//     queued records) resends every entry still open (its release not passed). An own entry goes once on the key it was
+//     made in; a taken one only on a later key (no re-broadcast). The remaining time goes with every send: the receiver
+//     keeps the release on its own clock (arrival + remaining), a relay sends what is left of it;
+//   - the activation blob: the buddy appends the open entries (not about the activated rank) after the UD table ("GAAD");
+//     the spare stores them and checks them only when its lineage view is complete (after its REJOIN_ACKs);
